{"strongs": "H4975", "word": "מָתְנַ֫יִם", "translit": "mo.ten", "root": "מתן", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine dual", "gloss": "loins", "definition": "מָתְנַ֫יִם noun masculine dual loins (Arabic back , the two sides of the back , etc.; Syriac ; — absolute ׳ מ Deut 33:11 + 7 t., מָתְנָ֑יִם Ezek 29:7 ; Ezek 47:4 construct מָתְנֵי Jer 13:11 + 3t.; suffix מָתְנַי Isa 21:3 , מָתְנָ֑י Jer 13:2 מָתְנֵיהֶם 1 Kings + Jer 20:32 + 4 t., etc.; — loins: 1. a. place of wearing girdle 1Kgs 2:5 ; 2Kgs 1:8 ; Jer 13:1 ; Jer 13:2 ; Jer 13:4 ; Jer 13:11 ; Ezek 23:15 figurative Isa 11:5 righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins . \\ \\ b. hence place of things attached to girdle: — sword girded on ( חגר על , אסר 2Sam 20:8 ; Neh 4:12 opposed to, וּמָתְנֵי מְלָכִים אֲפַתֵּחַ Isa 45:1 and the loins of kings I will loosen , i e. will disarm them ( ׳ י before Cyrus; compare Che ); ink-horn Ezek 9:2 ; Ezek 9:3 ; Ezek 9:11 . \\ \\ c. girding up loins = make ready for action, וַיְשַׁנֵּס מָתְנָיו 1Kgs 18:46 more often ׳ חָגַר מ 2Kgs 4:29 ; 2Kgs 9:1 ; Exod 12:11 ( P ), Dan 10:5 ׳ אָזַר מ Jer 1:17 . \\ \\ d. ׳ זַרְזִיר מ Prov 30:31 that which is girt in the loins , i.e. probably either a greyhound Ew Bö De (contracted, as if by a belt), or a war-horse, charger, Bo Ges Hi Str Wild (with a saddle); compare also זרזיר , p. 267 above; text perhaps corrupt ( Wild ). \\ \\ e. girded with sackcloth (in mourning) Gen 37:34 ( J ), Amos 8:10 ; Isa 20:2 ; 1Kgs 20:31 ; 1Kgs 20:32 ; Jer 48:37 . feminine linen breeches of priests were to extend מִמָּתְנַיִם וְעַד יְרֵכַיִם Exod 28:42 ( P ); to be ׳ עַלמָֿת Ezek 44:18 loins of slaves are girt with waistcloth, compare Job 12:18 (see also אֵזוֺר ). \\ \\ g. in general of the middle of the body, ׳ מֵי מָת Ezek 47:4 (i.e. water reaching to the loins); so of the appearance of ׳ י in Ezekiel's visions Ezek 1:27 (twice in verse); Ezek 8:2 (twice in verse). 2. a. loins as seat of strength, Deut 33:11 ; 1Kgs 12:10 = 2Chr 10:10 חַזֵּק מָתְנַיִם Nah 2:2 (|| אַמֵּץ כֹּחַ ); כֹּחוֺ בְּמָתְנָיו Job 40:16 (of hippopotamus); in combination with 1 a (figurative) חָֽגְרָה ׳ בְּעוֺז מ Prov 31:17 she girdeth her loins with strength , she puts on energy with her girdle; compare also ׳ בְּשִׁבְרוֺן מ Ezek 21:11 sigh with breaking of loins , i.e. in entire collapse of strength; so תָּמִיד ׳ הַמְעַ֑ד וּמ Ps 69:24 and make their loins continually to shake , make them totter; compare Ezek 29:7 (where read וְהִמְעַדְתָּ for וְהַעֲמַדְתָּ , see מָעַד ). \\ \\ b. as seat of keenest pain, due to grief or dread Nah 2:11 ; Isa 21:3 (as in travail); so probably also Ps 66:11 (compare Bae ; and see מוּעָקָה below עוק ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4899')\">BDB4899</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H4975')\">H4975</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4898')\">BDB4898</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4900')\">BDB4900</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>מָתְנַ֫יִם</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine dual</b> <highlightword>loins</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder3123/> <highlight>back</highlight>, <placeholder3124/> <highlight>the two sides of the back</highlight>, etc.; Syriac <placeholder3125/>; — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 33:11\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(5,33,11)\">Deut 33:11</ref> + 7 t., <bdbheb>מָתְנָ֑יִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 29:7\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(26,29,7)\">Ezek 29:7</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 47:4\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(26,47,4)\">Ezek 47:4</ref> construct <bdbheb>מָתְנֵי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 13:11\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(24,13,11)\">Jer 13:11</ref> + 3t.; suffix <bdbheb>מָתְנַי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 21:3\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(23,21,3)\">Isa 21:3</ref>, <bdbheb>מָתְנָ֑י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 13:2\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(24,13,2)\">Jer 13:2</ref> <bdbheb>מָתְנֵיהֶם</bdbheb> 1 Kings + <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Jer 20:32\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"32\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"32\" onclick=\"bcv(24,20,32)\">Jer 20:32</ref> + 4 t., etc.; — <highlight>loins:</highlight> <div class=\"point\"><b>1. a.</b> <highlightword>place of wearing girdle</highlightword> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 2:5\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(11,2,5)\">1Kgs 2:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 1:8\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(12,1,8)\">2Kgs 1:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 13:1\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(24,13,1)\">Jer 13:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 13:2\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(24,13,2)\">Jer 13:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 13:4\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(24,13,4)\">Jer 13:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 13:11\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(24,13,11)\">Jer 13:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 23:15\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(26,23,15)\">Ezek 23:15</ref> figurative <ref ref=\"Isa 11:5\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(23,11,5)\">Isa 11:5</ref> <highlight>righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins</highlight>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> hence place of things attached to girdle: — sword girded on (<bdbheb>חגר על</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אסר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Sam 20:8\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(10,20,8)\">2Sam 20:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Neh 4:12\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(16,4,12)\">Neh 4:12</ref> opposed to, <bdbheb>וּמָתְנֵי מְלָכִים אֲפַתֵּחַ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 45:1\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"45\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"45\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(23,45,1)\">Isa 45:1</ref> <highlight>and the loins of kings I will loosen</highlight>, i e. will disarm them (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> before Cyrus; compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Che')\">Che</lookup>); ink-horn <ref ref=\"Ezek 9:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,9,2)\">Ezek 9:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 9:3\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(26,9,3)\">Ezek 9:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 9:11\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(26,9,11)\">Ezek 9:11</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>c.</b> girding up <highlight>loins</highlight> = make ready for action, <bdbheb>וַיְשַׁנֵּס</bdbheb> <bdbheb>מָתְנָיו</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 18:46\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"46\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"46\" onclick=\"bcv(11,18,46)\">1Kgs 18:46</ref> more often <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>חָגַר מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Kgs 4:29\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(12,4,29)\">2Kgs 4:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Kgs 9:1\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(12,9,1)\">2Kgs 9:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 12:11\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(2,12,11)\">Exod 12:11</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Dan 10:5\" b=\"27\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(27,10,5)\">Dan 10:5</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>אָזַר מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 1:17\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(24,1,17)\">Jer 1:17</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>d.</b> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>זַרְזִיר מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 30:31\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(20,30,31)\">Prov 30:31</ref> that which is <highlight>girt in the loins</highlight>, i.e. probably either a <highlight>greyhound</highlight> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Bö')\">Bö</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup> (contracted, as if by a belt), or a war-horse, charger, <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Bo')\">Bo</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hi')\">Hi</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Str')\">Str</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Wild')\">Wild</lookup> (with a saddle); compare also <bdbheb>זרזיר</bdbheb>, p. 267 above; text perhaps corrupt (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Wild')\">Wild</lookup>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>e.</b> girded with sackcloth (in mourning) <ref ref=\"Gen 37:34\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(1,37,34)\">Gen 37:34</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Amos 8:10\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(30,8,10)\">Amos 8:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 20:2\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(23,20,2)\">Isa 20:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 20:31\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(11,20,31)\">1Kgs 20:31</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 20:32\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"32\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"32\" onclick=\"bcv(11,20,32)\">1Kgs 20:32</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 48:37\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"37\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"37\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,37)\">Jer 48:37</ref>. <b>feminine</b> <highlightword>linen breeches of priests were to extend</highlightword> <bdbheb>מִמָּתְנַיִם וְעַד</bdbheb> <bdbheb>יְרֵכַיִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 28:42\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"42\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"42\" onclick=\"bcv(2,28,42)\">Exod 28:42</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>); to be <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>עַלמָֿת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 44:18\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(26,44,18)\">Ezek 44:18</ref> loins of slaves are girt with waistcloth, compare <ref ref=\"Job 12:18\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(18,12,18)\">Job 12:18</ref> (see also <bdbheb>אֵזוֺר</bdbheb>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>g.</b> in general of the middle of the body, <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מֵי מָת</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 47:4\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(26,47,4)\">Ezek 47:4</ref> (i.e. water reaching to the loins); so of the appearance of <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> in Ezekiel's visions <ref ref=\"Ezek 1:27\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(26,1,27)\">Ezek 1:27</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Ezek 8:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,8,2)\">Ezek 8:2</ref> (twice in verse). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2. a.</b> <highlight>loins</highlight> as seat of strength, <ref ref=\"Deut 33:11\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(5,33,11)\">Deut 33:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 12:10\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(11,12,10)\">1Kgs 12:10</ref> = <ref ref=\"2Chr 10:10\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(14,10,10)\">2Chr 10:10</ref> <bdbheb>חַזֵּק מָתְנַיִם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Nah 2:2\" b=\"34\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(34,2,2)\">Nah 2:2</ref> (|| <bdbheb>אַמֵּץ כֹּחַ</bdbheb>); <bdbheb>כֹּחוֺ בְּמָתְנָיו</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Job 40:16\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(18,40,16)\">Job 40:16</ref> (of hippopotamus); in combination with <b>1 a</b> (figurative) <bdbheb>חָֽגְרָה</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>בְּעוֺז מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Prov 31:17\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(20,31,17)\">Prov 31:17</ref> <highlight>she girdeth her loins with strength</highlight>, she puts on energy with her girdle; compare also <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>בְּשִׁבְרוֺן מ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 21:11\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(26,21,11)\">Ezek 21:11</ref> sigh <highlight>with breaking of loins</highlight>, i.e. in entire collapse of strength; so <bdbheb>תָּמִיד</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הַמְעַ֑ד וּמ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 69:24\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"69\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"69\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(19,69,24)\">Ps 69:24</ref> <highlight>and make their loins continually to shake</highlight>, make them totter; compare <ref ref=\"Ezek 29:7\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"29\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"29\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(26,29,7)\">Ezek 29:7</ref> (where read <bdbheb>וְהִמְעַדְתָּ</bdbheb> for <bdbheb>וְהַעֲמַדְתָּ</bdbheb>, see  <bdbheb><reflink>מָעַד</reflink></bdbheb>). <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> as seat of keenest pain, due to grief or dread <ref ref=\"Nah 2:11\" b=\"34\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(34,2,11)\">Nah 2:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 21:3\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(23,21,3)\">Isa 21:3</ref> (as in travail); so probably also <ref ref=\"Ps 66:11\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"66\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"66\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(19,66,11)\">Ps 66:11</ref> (compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Bae')\">Bae</lookup>; and see  <bdbheb><reflink>מוּעָקָה</reflink></bdbheb> below <bdbheb>עוק</bdbheb>). </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Deut 33:11", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 33, "verse": 11}, {"raw": "Ezek 29:7", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 29, "verse": 7}, {"raw": "Ezek 47:4", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 47, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "Jer 13:11", "book": "JER", "chapter": 13, "verse": 11}, {"raw": "Isa 21:3", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 21, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Jer 13:2", "book": "JER", "chapter": 13, "verse": 2}, {"raw": "Jer 20:32", "book": "JER", "chapter": 20, "verse": 32}, {"raw": "1Kgs 2:5", "book": "1KI", "chapter": 2, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "2Kgs 1:8", "book": "2KI",